{"id":"mahabharata-12-014","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":14,"title":"चतुर्दशोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 14 · Draupadi's plea","summary":{"en":"Draupadi reminds Yudhishthira of his promises and of the sufferings of the exile, and tells him that the kingdom must be governed with the rod of punishment. She urges him to enjoy the earth and perform sacrifices.","kn":"ದ್ರೌಪದಿ ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರನಿಗೆ ಅವನ ವಾಗ್ದಾನ, ವನವಾಸದ ಕಷ್ಟಗಳನ್ನು ನೆನಪಿಸಿ ರಾಜ್ಯವನ್ನು ದಂಡದಿಂದ ಆಳಬೇಕೆನ್ನುತ್ತಾಳೆ. ಭೂಮಿಯನ್ನು ಅನುಭವಿಸಿ ಯಜ್ಞ ಮಾಡುವಂತೆ ಒತ್ತಾಯಿಸುತ್ತಾಳೆ.","hi":"द्रौपदी युधिष्ठिर को उनके वचनों और वनवास के कष्टों की याद दिलाती हैं और कहती हैं कि राज्य दण्ड से चलाया जाता है। वे उनसे पृथ्वी का भोग करने और यज्ञ करने का आग्रह करती हैं।","te":"ద్రౌపది యుధిష్ఠిరునికి అతని వాగ్దానాలను, వనవాస కష్టాలను గుర్తు చేసి రాజ్యాన్ని దండంతో పాలించాలని అంటుంది. భూమిని అనుభవించి యజ్ఞాలు చేయమని కోరుతుంది.","ta":"திரௌபதி யுதிஷ்டிரருக்கு அவர் வாக்குறுதிகளையும் வனவாசத் துயரங்களையும் நினைவூட்டி, நாடு தண்டத்தால் ஆளப்பட வேண்டும் என்கிறாள். நிலத்தை அனுபவித்து வேள்விகள் செய்யும்படி வேண்டுகிறாள்.","ml":"യുധിഷ്ഠിരന്റെ വാഗ്ദാനങ്ങളും വനവാസത്തിലെ ദുരിതങ്ങളും ദ്രൗപദി ഓർമ്മിപ്പിക്കുന്നു; ശിക്ഷയുടെ ദണ്ഡുകൊണ്ട് രാജ്യം ഭരിക്കണമെന്ന് അവർ പറയുന്നു. ഭൂമി അനുഭവിക്കാനും യജ്ഞങ്ങൾ ചെയ്യാനും അവർ അദ്ദേഹത്തോട് ആവശ്യപ്പെടുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.14; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"राजधर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Rajadharma Parva (Duties of kings)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"अव्याहरति कौन्तेये धर्मराजे युधिष्ठिरे ।\nभ्रातॄणां ब्रुवतां तांस्तान्विविधान्वेदनिश्चयान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"While Yudhishthira, Kunti's son and king of dharma, said nothing, his brothers kept speaking, each in turn, of various Vedic conclusions."}},{"n":2,"text":"महाभिजनसंपन्ना श्रीमत्यायतलोचना ।\nअभ्यभाषत राजेन्द्रं द्रौपदी योषितां वरा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then Draupadi, best of women, of great lineage, radiant, with wide eyes, spoke to the best of kings."}},{"n":3,"text":"आसीनमृषभं राज्ञां भ्रातृभिः परिवारितम् ।\nसिंहशार्दूलसदृशैर्वारणैरिव यूथपम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"He sat there, the bull among kings, surrounded by his brothers, who were like lions and tigers, like elephants around the leader of the herd."}},{"n":4,"text":"अभिमानवती नित्यं विशेषेण युधिष्ठिरे ।\nलालिता सततं राज्ञा धर्मज्ञा धर्मदर्शिनी ॥","meaning":{"en":"She was always proud, and especially so of Yudhishthira, and the king had always cherished her; she knew dharma and saw it clearly."}},{"n":5,"text":"आमन्त्र्य विपुलश्रोणी साम्ना परमवल्गुना ।\nभर्तारमभिसंप्रेक्ष्य ततो वचनमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That broad-hipped lady addressed her husband with very gentle, soothing words, looking at him, and then spoke."}},{"n":6,"text":"इमे ते भ्रातरः पार्थ शुष्यन्त स्तोकका इव ।\nवावाश्यमानास्तिष्ठन्ति न चैनानभिनन्दसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Draupadi said: Partha, these brothers of yours are drying up like cataka birds crying out for rain, and they stand calling to you, yet you do not cheer them."}},{"n":7,"text":"नन्दयैतान्महाराज मत्तानिव महाद्विपान् ।\nउपपन्नेन वाक्येन सततं दुःखभागिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Great king, gladden them, who have always shared in your sorrow, with fitting words, as one soothes maddened great elephants."}},{"n":8,"text":"कथं द्वैतवने राजन्पूर्वमुक्त्वा तथा वचः ।\nभ्रातॄनेतान्स्म सहिताञ्शीतवातातपार्दितान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"King, how could you, in the Dvaita forest, speak as you did to these same brothers, who were worn down together by cold, wind and sun?"}},{"n":9,"text":"वयं दुर्योधनं हत्वा मृधे भोक्ष्याम मेदिनीम् ।\nसंपूर्णां सर्वकामानामाहवे विजयैषिणः ॥","meaning":{"en":"You said, \"We shall kill Duryodhana in battle and enjoy the earth, full of every desire, seeking victory in the fight;"}},{"n":10,"text":"विरथांश्च रथान्कृत्वा निहत्य च महागजान् ।\nसंस्तीर्य च रथैर्भूमिं ससादिभिररिंदमाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"tormentors of foes, we shall leave chariots without riders, kill great elephants, and cover the earth with chariots and horsemen,"}},{"n":11,"text":"यजतां विविधैर्यज्ञैः समृद्धैराप्तदक्षिणैः ।\nवनवासकृतं दुःखं भविष्यति सुखाय नः ॥","meaning":{"en":"and sacrifice with many rich sacrifices with full fees. The suffering of living in the forest will turn to happiness for us.\""}},{"n":12,"text":"इत्येतानेवमुक्त्वा त्वं स्वयं धर्मभृतां वर ।\nकथमद्य पुनर्वीर विनिहंसि मनांस्युत ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having said all that to them, best of those who uphold dharma, how is it that you now break their hearts again, hero?"}},{"n":13,"text":"न क्लीबो वसुधां भुङ्क्ते न क्लीबो धनमश्नुते ।\nन क्लीबस्य गृहे पुत्रा मत्स्याः पङ्क इवासते ॥","meaning":{"en":"A eunuch does not enjoy the earth, a eunuch does not gain wealth, and the sons of a eunuch's house sit like fish in mud."}},{"n":14,"text":"नादण्डः क्षत्रियो भाति नादण्डो भूतिमश्नुते ।\nनादण्डस्य प्रजा राज्ञः सुखमेधन्ति भारत ॥","meaning":{"en":"A kshatriya without the rod of punishment does not shine; one without the rod does not win prosperity; and, Bharata, the subjects of a king without the rod do not thrive in happiness."}},{"n":15,"text":"मित्रता सर्वभूतेषु दानमध्ययनं तपः ।\nब्राह्मणस्यैष धर्मः स्यान्न राज्ञो राजसत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Friendliness to all beings, giving, study and austerity may be the dharma of a brahmin, but not of a king, best of kings."}},{"n":16,"text":"असतां प्रतिषेधश्च सतां च परिपालनम् ।\nएष राज्ञां परो धर्मः समरे चापलायनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Restraining the wicked, protecting the good, and not fleeing in battle: this is the highest dharma of kings."}},{"n":17,"text":"यस्मिन्क्षमा च क्रोधश्च दानादाने भयाभये ।\nनिग्रहानुग्रहौ चोभौ स वै धर्मविदुच्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"He in whom forgiveness and anger, giving and taking, fearlessness and fear, punishing and favoring are all found is called one who knows dharma."}},{"n":18,"text":"न श्रुतेन न दानेन न सान्त्वेन न चेज्यया ।\nत्वयेयं पृथिवी लब्धा नोत्कोचेन तथाप्युत ॥","meaning":{"en":"You did not win this earth by learning, nor by giving, nor by conciliation, nor by sacrifice, nor even by bribery."}},{"n":19,"text":"यत्तद्बलममित्राणां तथा वीरसमुद्यतम् ।\nहस्त्यश्वरथसंपन्नं त्रिभिरङ्गैर्महत्तरम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"That enemy force, raised by heroes, well supplied with elephants, horses and chariots, and the greater for its three arms,"}},{"n":20,"text":"रक्षितं द्रोणकर्णाभ्यामश्वत्थाम्ना कृपेण च ।\nतत्त्वया निहतं वीर तस्माद्भुङ्क्ष्व वसुंधराम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"guarded by Drona, Karna, Ashvatthaman and Kripa, was destroyed by you, hero. So enjoy the earth."}},{"n":21,"text":"जम्बूद्वीपो महाराज नानाजनपदायुतः ।\nत्वया पुरुषशार्दूल दण्डेन मृदितः प्रभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"Great king, Jambudvipa with its many tens of thousands of lands, tiger among men, was crushed by your rod."}},{"n":22,"text":"जम्बूद्वीपेन सदृशः क्रौञ्चद्वीपो नराधिप ।\nअपरेण महामेरोर्दण्डेन मृदितस्त्वया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Krauncha-dvipa, equal to Jambudvipa, lord of men, to the west of Mount Meru, was crushed by your rod."}},{"n":23,"text":"क्रौञ्चद्वीपेन सदृशः शाकद्वीपो नराधिप ।\nपूर्वेण तु महामेरोर्दण्डेन मृदितस्त्वया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Shakadvipa, equal to Krauncha-dvipa, lord of men, to the east of Mount Meru, was crushed by your rod."}},{"n":24,"text":"उत्तरेण महामेरोः शाकद्वीपेन संमितः ।\nभद्राश्वः पुरुषव्याघ्र दण्डेन मृदितस्त्वया ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhadrashva, tiger among men, matching Shakadvipa, to the north of Mount Meru, was crushed by your rod."}},{"n":25,"text":"द्वीपाश्च सान्तरद्वीपा नानाजनपदालयाः ।\nविगाह्य सागरं वीर दण्डेन मृदितास्त्वया ॥","meaning":{"en":"The islands and the lesser islands, home to many peoples, you crossed the ocean and crushed with your rod, hero."}},{"n":26,"text":"एतान्यप्रतिमानि त्वं कृत्वा कर्माणि भारत ।\nन प्रीयसे महाराज पूज्यमानो द्विजातिभिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having done these matchless deeds, Bharata, great king, you are not pleased even though brahmins honor you."}},{"n":27,"text":"स त्वं भ्रातॄनिमान्दृष्ट्वा प्रतिनन्दस्व भारत ।\nऋषभानिव संमत्तान्गजेन्द्रानूर्जितानिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"So look at these brothers of yours, Bharata, and answer their joy, as you would bulls in rut or mighty lords of elephants."}},{"n":28,"text":"अमरप्रतिमाः सर्वे शत्रुसाहाः परंतपाः ।\nएकोऽपि हि सुखायैषां क्षमः स्यादिति मे मतिः ॥","meaning":{"en":"All of them are like immortals, enduring against foes and tormentors of enemies. In my view even one of them could bring happiness."}},{"n":29,"text":"किं पुनः पुरुषव्याघ्राः पतयो मे नरर्षभाः ।\nसमस्तानीन्द्रियाणीव शरीरस्य विचेष्टने ॥","meaning":{"en":"How much more my husbands, these tigers among men and bulls among men, who are like all the senses together moving the body."}},{"n":30,"text":"अनृतं माब्रवीच्छ्वश्रूः सर्वज्ञा सर्वदर्शिनी ।\nयुधिष्ठिरस्त्वां पाञ्चालि सुखे धास्यत्यनुत्तमे ॥","meaning":{"en":"My mother-in-law, who knows all and sees all, did not speak falsely: \"Yudhishthira will set you, Panchali, in the highest happiness.\""}},{"n":31,"text":"हत्वा राजसहस्राणि बहून्याशुपराक्रमः ।\nतद्व्यर्थं संप्रपश्यामि मोहात्तव जनाधिप ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having killed many thousands of kings with swift valor, I see that all as futile, lord of the people, because of your delusion."}},{"n":32,"text":"येषामुन्मत्तको ज्येष्ठः सर्वे तस्योपचारिणः ।\nतवोन्मादेन राजेन्द्र सोन्मादाः सर्वपाण्डवाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"When the eldest is mad, all who serve him are mad too. Through your madness, king of kings, all the Pandavas are mad."}},{"n":33,"text":"यदि हि स्युरनुन्मत्ता भ्रातरस्ते जनाधिप ।\nबद्ध्वा त्वां नास्तिकैः सार्धं प्रशासेयुर्वसुंधराम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"If your brothers were not mad, lord of the people, they would bind you along with the unbelievers and rule the earth themselves."}},{"n":34,"text":"कुरुते मूढमेवं हि यः श्रेयो नाधिगच्छति ।\nधूपैरञ्जनयोगैश्च नस्यकर्मभिरेव च ।\nभेषजैः स चिकित्स्यः स्याद्य उन्मार्गेण गच्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"A man who acts so foolishly and does not find the good should be treated with fumigations, ointments, snuffs and medicines, as one who has strayed from the path."}},{"n":35,"text":"साहं सर्वाधमा लोके स्त्रीणां भरतसत्तम ।\nतथा विनिकृतामित्रैर्याहमिच्छामि जीवितुम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"I am the lowest of women in the world, best of the Bharatas, so wronged by enemies, and yet I wish to live."}},{"n":36,"text":"एतेषां यतमानानामुत्पद्यन्ते तु संपदः ।\nत्वं तु सर्वां महीं लब्ध्वा कुरुषे स्वयमापदम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"For those who strive, prosperity comes; but you, having won the whole earth, make a calamity for yourself."}},{"n":37,"text":"यथास्तां संमतौ राज्ञां पृथिव्यां राजसत्तमौ ।\nमान्धाता चाम्बरीषश्च तथा राजन्विराजसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"As Mandhatri and Ambarisha, two best of kings, were honored among kings on earth, so you shine, O king."}},{"n":38,"text":"प्रशाधि पृथिवीं देवीं प्रजा धर्मेण पालयन् ।\nसपर्वतवनद्वीपां मा राजन्विमना भव ॥","meaning":{"en":"Rule the divine earth, protecting the people by dharma, with her mountains, forests and islands. Do not be low in spirit, O king."}},{"n":39,"text":"यजस्व विविधैर्यज्ञैर्जुह्वन्नग्नीन्प्रयच्छ च ।\nपुराणि भोगान्वासांसि द्विजातिभ्यो नृपोत्तम ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sacrifice with many kinds of sacrifice, offering into the fires, and give cities, enjoyments and garments to the twice-born, best of kings."}}]}]}